-- Ordered quest guidance; source 967020b2b8ca645afcaf90d9bbe5a1b64673947d; generated 2026-10-20.
QuestGuidance.Register("en",112,{
[3553]="7002CCFE\n1\tCollect goat-hides in the Wailing Hills (total: 10)\tWild goats can be found throughout the Wailing Hills. Frithstan has asked you to hunt the wild goats of the Wailing Hills for their hides.\n2\tReturn the hides to Frithstan\tFrithstan is at his camp near the Cuthstan. You should return to Frithstan with news of your success.\n",
[3554]="700359B3\n1\tMake warming winter stew for the refugees (quantity: see journal)\tYou have been given the recipe for a warming winter stew. You should make a warming winter stew to feed the refugees for Wildermore.\n2\tDeliver the warming winter stew to Hildeleth\tHildelith is in Forlaw. You have made warming winter stew and should now deliver it to Hildelith.\n",
[3555]="7006753B\n1\tComplete Quest 'Cooking Catastrophe: Drake Eggs'\030Complete Quest 'Cooking Catastrophe: Beetle Larvae'\tComplete two tasks for Shulgolb at Kafagur.\n2\tTalk to Shulgolb at Kafagur\tYou've helped Shulgolb collect enough ingredients. You should talk to him at Kafagur.\n3\tTalk to Uzhún\tShulgolb has given you the ingredients that Uzhún requires. Uzhún can be found at Kafagur.\n",
[3556]="7006753A\n1\tCollect larvae from beetle nests on Ghax-hophra (total: 6)\tShulgolb has asked you to collect larvae from beetle nests on Ghax-hophra. Ghax-hophra is located north of Kafagur.\n2\tTalk to Shulgolb at Kafagur\tYou've collected a good amount of beetle larvae. You should bring them to Shulgolb at Kafagur.\n",
[3557]="70067542\n1\tCollect eggs from drake nests in Jeb Lipha (total: 6)\tShulgolb has asked you to collect drake eggs from nests in Jeb Lipha. Jeb Lipha is located east of Kafagur.\n2\tTalk to Shulgolb at Kafagur\tYou've collected a good amount of drake eggs. You should bring them to Shulgolb at Kafagur.\n",
[3558]="70067541\n1\tSearch provision barrels for Uzhún's salt pouch\tUzhún has asked you to search for their salt pouch. It must be in one of the provision barrels around Kafagur.\n2\tTalk to Uzhún\tYou've found Uzhún's salt pouch. They wait for you at Kafagur.\n",
[3559]="7000AC4E\n1\tDeliver the oil to Soldier Glat at Tol Ascarnen\030Collect Barrel of Oil (total: 5)\tOil can be found on the Free Peoples fighting throughout the Ettenmoors. The closest camp is over the southern bridge, though a larger group can be found at Ost Ringdyr, far to the east. Angmar's Army is shoring up the defences at Tol Ascarnen. Glat needs oil with which to douse the Free Peoples who attempt to assail the keep.\n",
[3560]="700461A7\n1\tCollect the jug of cool water\tA jug of water can be found near Tansy Tighfield at the Party Tree. You should collect the jug of water.\n2\tOverheated patrons can be found throughout Hobbiton. You should use the water creatively to help cool off overheated patrons.\t\n3\tReturn to Tansy Tighfield\tTansy Tighfield can be found at the party tree in Hobbiton. You should speak with Tansy Tighfield.\n",
[3561]="7001931F\n1\tDeliver the wood to Bregedúr in Celondim\tDeliver the cask wood to Bregedúr at the crafting tier at Celondim. Collecting the wood was half of the journey. Now you must deliver the material to the craftsman who shall make the cask for Elven wine.\n",
[3562]="70059255\n1\tCollect Copper Coins of Gundabad (total: 30)\tCollect 30 Copper Coins of Gundabad to trade with the March on Gundabad Quartermaster. This quest can be completed weekly.\n2\tTalk to the March on Gundabad Quartermaster to trade Copper Coins of Gundabad for Motes. This quest can be completed weekly.\t\n",
[3563]="7005976C\n1\tCollect copper ore in the Wildwood (total: 10)\tCopper ore can be found in the Wildwood. You should collect copper ore.\n2\tPlace the copper ore in a storage crate\tA storage crate can be found in either Trader's Wharf or Trestlebridge. You should place the copper ore in a storage crate.\n",
[3564]="700579F8\n1\tTalk to Thorían\tThorían is in central Duillond, near the workbenches. You should go and ask Thorían for handfasting cords.\n2\tCollect a bolt of silk\tThe bolt of silk is in a crate at Brethilas' shop in Duillond. You should get a bolt of silk and bring it to be cut at the tailor's workbench.\n3\tCut the silk bolt into ribbons (total: 5)\tCut the silk cloth into ribbons at Thorían's workbench in Duillond. You should cut the silk into pretty ribbons.\n4\tTalk to Thorían\tThorían is in central Duillond, near the workbenches. You should bring the cut ribbons to Thorían.\n5\tTalk to Dringlaer in Duillond\030Collect perfect blossoms (total: 10)\tThe metalsmith Dringlaer can be found in central Duillond, and the flowers bloom in and around the city. Thorían asked you to gather flowers and speak to Dringlaer.\n6\tTalk to Thorían\tThorían can be found in Duillond. You have gathered the charms and flowers. Return to Thorían.\n7\tConstruct the handfasting cords\t\n8\tDeliver the completed handfasting cords to Celairel\tCelairel is south of Duillond. Bring the handfasting cords to Celairel.\n",
[3565]="700544B0\n1\tDefeat wights in Minas Morgul (total: 12)\030Defeat deadly sorrow-wights in Minas Morgul (total: 8)\tWights can be found in the Circle of Sorrow in Minas Morgul. You should defeat any wights that you find.\n2\tTalk to Damrod\tDamrod can be found in Barad Orhant in Minas Morgul. You should talk to Damrod.\n",
[3566]="700097D6\n1\tDefeat salamanders on Tyl Ruinen (total: 10)\tThe islands of Tyl Ruinen are located north-east of Rushingdale, near the middle of the lake, in Evendim. Gwindeth has asked you to defeat the corrupted salamanders you find on Tyl Ruinen.\n2\tTalk to Gwindeth\tThe Blue Lady is in Gwindethrond, behind the waterfall at Rushingdale in western Emyn Uial, south-west of Tyl Ruinen. Gwindeth is waiting to hear that you have dealt a blow to the salamanders of Tyl Ruinen.\n",
[3567]="7005C8A7\n1\tDefeat hobgoblin captains (total: 4)\030Defeat Tuzugrák\030Recover the candle\tTuzugrák and the hobgolins can be found holed up in Anatrâd. Lore-master Rúni has asked you to defeat Tuzugrák and his hobgoblin captains, and to bring back the stolen candle.\n2\tReturn to Rúni\tLore-master Rúni is in Bazanmanar, in the north-east Clovengap. You should bring the candle to Rúni.\n",
[3568]="70058418\n1\tCollect strange crystals (total: 12)\tHowlers' Notch is north-west of Annâk-khurfu. Mother Amma has asked you to collect more of the fell crystals.\n2\tTalk to Mother Amma\tMother Amma is in the forge at Annâk-khurfu, in southern Elderslade. You should bring the crystals to Mother Amma.\n3\tPut the crystals into the chest\tThe chest is located near the forge at Annâk-khurfu. Mother Amma has asked you to place the foul smelling crystals in a chest.\n4\tTalk to Mother Amma\tMother Amma is in the forge at Annâk-khurfu. You should talk to Mother Amma.\n5\tTalk to Gunvald\tGunvald is in Annâk-khurfu. Mother Amma has asked you to pass a message along to Gunvald.\n6\tReturn to Mother Amma\tMother Amma is in the forge of Annâk-khurfu. Gunvald has asked you to give his thanks to Mother Amma.\n",
[3569]="7003EA77\n1\tDefeat bog-lurkers in the North Trollshaws (total: 8)\tBog-lurkers can be found in the Gladdalf, in the North Trollshaws. Thoroniel has asked you and your companions to put down the bog-lurkers of the North Trollshaws.\n2\tTalk to Thoroniel\tThoroniel is posted to the south and west of the Gladdalf in the North Trollshaws. You should return to Thoroniel and let her know that you have done as she has asked.\n",
[3570]="7001AACB\n1\tDestroy corrupted relics (total: 6)\tThe corrupted relics lie within Minas Gîl, east of Ost Galadh. Agorin has asked you to destroy the corrupted Silvan relics within Minas Gîl.\n2\tTalk to Agorin at Ost Galadh\tAgorin is at Ost Galadh, west of Minas Gîl. You should report your success to Agorin.\n",
[3571]="7002F990\n1\tKill crazed salamanders (total: 10)\tCrazed salamanders can be found roaming the bog near Harwick. You should kill crazed salamanders in the bog, and observe their strange behaviour.\n2\tDiscover the source of the salamanders' strange behaviour\tCrazed salamanders can be found roaming the bog near Harwick. You should try to discover the source of the strange behaviour in the salamanders.\n3\tCompleted\tThe source of the crazed behaviour in the salamanders seems to have something to do with draugar coming out the cave ahead....\n",
[3572]="70032BE0\n1\tDefeat globsnaga spiders (total: 7)\tThe oddly shaped shadows that Knakk referred to can be found to the east and south-east of where he is camped, up on the elevated walkway in the north-east corner of Redhorn Lodes.\n2\tReturn to Knakk\tKnakk is camped on the elevated walkway in the north-east corner of Redhorn Lodes. He will be eager to hear what you found while exploring the eastern side of Redhorn Lodes.\n",
[3573]="7005B8D7\n1\tDefeat Crágacha\tThe Angmarim priest can be found in north-western Clovengap. You should find and defeat the priest who is working to corrupt the deserting Angmarim.\n2\tReturn to Mother Amma\tMother Amma is in Bazanmanar, in north-east Clovengap. You should bring the new fragment to Mother Amma.\n",
[3574]="7005C550\n1\tMissing scouts can be found in Gadh Ujáf, Zagâf Muzug, and Rung-shakam. You should look for, and rescue, the missing scouts.\t\n2\tReturn to Mother Amma\tMother Amma is in Bazanmanar, in north-east Clovengap. You should tell Mother Amma that you freed the Angmarim deserters.\n",
[3575]="700228A7\n1\tInvestigate cairn-stones (total: 6)\tThe corrupted cairn-stones lie to the north of Trac-plas, south-west of Mincham's camp. Mincham asked you to seek out corrupted cairn-stones, examine them, and report back with your findings.\n2\tTalk to Mincham in the Lich Bluffs\tMincham's camp is north-east of Trac-plas. You should return to Mincham and report that you discovered a strange liquid had been poured on the cairn-stones, and that several dark markings were engraved upon them as well.\n",
[3576]="7000E835\n1\tScout Ost Guruth\tOst Guruth lies in the Lone-lands, far to the east of Bree-land, along the Great East Road. Nidgyl has told you to begin your patrol of the Lone-lands at the stronghold of Ost Guruth.\n2\tScout Ost Haer\tOst Haer lies in the Grimfens in the Lone-lands, south of Ost Guruth, far to the east of Bree-land. Nidgyl has asked you to scout the ruins of Ost Haer.\n3\tScout Dol Vaeg\tDol Vaeg lies in the Lone-lands, far to the east of Bree-land, west of the Last Bridge. Nidgyl has asked you to climb the spire of Dol Vaeg, a tall hill some ways to the west of the Last Bridge. It offers an excellent view of the surrounding lands.\n4\tScout Nan Dhelu\tNan Dhelu lies in the Lone-lands, far to the east of Bree-land, north-east of Dol Vaeg. Nidgyl has asked you to scout the ruins of Nan Dhelu.\n5\tTalk to Nidgyl\tNidgyl is at Bree-town in Bree-land, far to the west of the Lone-lands. You should report to Nidgyl and tell him what you have found in the eastern Lone-lands.\n",
[3577]="70062978\n1\tInvestigate the corrupted plant\tGwenfor Mellion tells you the plants are wilting, and a shadow looming over the wild in the forest to the south-east. The forest she speaks of can be found south-east of Glyn Helyg. You can follow the road out of the village.\n2\tTalk to Gwenfor\tGwenfor awaits your report. Gwenfor can be found in Glyn Helyg.\n3\tVenture deeper into the forest\tGwenfor Mellion wants you to go deeper into the forest and confirm her suspicions. Continue further down the path to the south-east across the bridge. A faint shadow lingers around still waters.\n4\tDefeat the corrupted beast\tThe shadow has revealed itself.\n5\tTalk to Gwenfor\tThe corruption deeper in the forest has gone on to affect even the beasts. You should tell Gwenfor in Glyn Helyg immediately.\n6\tTalk to Nuddo Sutchic\tNuddo Sutchic can be found in Lintrev to the north. Gwenfor has asked you to share your findings with them.\n",
[3578]="700587A3\n1\tBrágha Fellwinder has gone to the tower of Caivád Sâr, in central Elderslade. You should defeat Brágha Fellwinder before she can pass on the knowledge of the crystals and the corruption her spells bring.\t\n2\tTalk to Gunvald\tGunvald is in Annâk-khurfu in Elderslade. Return to Gunvald.\n",
[3579]="7005B519\n1\tThe source of the crystals' corruption has been located, but what lies in wait in the muck?\t\n2\tReturn to Mother Amma\tMother Amma is in north-eastern Clovengap. You should tell Mother Amma that the threat has been defeated.\n",
[3580]="7005A691\n1\tGo to the next location\tDági has asked you to go to the next set of collection buckets and stop the Orc. The buckets are in an area that overlooks the Mirrormere, to the south-west of Ashmargathâl.\n2\tPretend to collect snow\030Defeat the Orc responsible\tThe Orc has not touched these buckets yet, but is most likely nearby. You should feign ignorance about the Orc's presence and pretend to collect snow.\n3\tTalk to Dági\tThis specific Orc will trouble Dági no longer. He waits for you at Ashmargathâl.\n",
[3581]="70065EA2\n1\tSpeak with Bárzqhosh at Grothum for advice\tMake your way to Grothum and speak with Taskmaster Bárzqhosh. Ask him for his design for making your sapling grow.\n2\tDeliver aurochs droppings to Cinaid at Gramsfoot\030Collect aurochs droppings ([see journal]/7)\tBárzqhosh provided a very strange answer. Go to the plains along the Hoardale where the Thistledown Grazers roam and collect their dung. Use it in the soil to grow your sapling.\n",
[3582]="70065EAC\n1\tSpeak with Bok at Grothum\tMake your way to Grothum and speak with the leader Bok to learn how the goblins would go about perverting the natural order that would grow this sapling.\n2\tDeliver the barrels of oil to Cinaid at Gramsfoot\030Collect barrels of oil ([see journal]/7)\tGo into the Ettenmoors and hunt down any of the Free Folk guards there. They will likely carry oil that can be used to poison the roots of the sapling. Replace water with oil and watch the sapling become rancid.\n",
[3583]="70065EB1\n1\tSpeak with Tyrant Bûrzgoth at Grothum\tMake your way to Grothum and ask Tyrant Bûrzgoth for guidance on how to corrupt the sapling.\n2\tCollect Morningthaw haunches ([see journal]/7)\tBûrzgoth suggested killing bears for their haunches and feeding them to your to your sapling... not a terrible idea from a troll.\n3\tDeliver Morningthaw haunches to Cinaid at Gramsfoot\tBûrzgoth suggested killing bears for their haunches and feeding them to your to your sapling... not a terrible idea from a troll.\n",
[3584]="70066678\n1\tDespoil the first location along the Hoardale River\030Despoil the second location along the Hoardale River\030Despoil the third location along the Hoardale River\030Despoil the fourth location along the Hoardale River\030Despoil the fifth location along the Hoardale River\tCinaid sent you into the Ettenmoors to target locations along the Hoardale where the Free Folk are looking to collect pure water. You are to befoul the water with poison to thwart the Free People's designs.\n2\tTalk to Cinaid\tThe water is poisoned and any collected here will surely not assist in the pure growth of anything that it feeds. Return to Cinaid at Gramsfoot and tell him of your success.\n",
})
